<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
        <title>{% block title %}LogHub{% endblock %}</title>
        <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 32 32%22><rect width=%2232%22 height=%2232%22 rx=%228%22 fill=%22%23111827%22/><g stroke=%22%23fff%22 stroke-width=%222.5%22 stroke-linecap=%22round%22><path d=%22M9 11h14M9 16h14M9 21h9%22/></g></svg>">
        {% block stylesheets %}{% endblock %}

        {% block javascripts %}
            {% block importmap %}{{ importmap('app') }}{% endblock %}
        {% endblock %}
    </head>
    <body class="min-h-dvh bg-canvas text-ink">
        <!--
        THESIS: A log console is judged on how fast the eye finds the one line that
        explains the incident. Refuses the dashboard arrangement: no cards, no
        decorative charts, no chrome stealing pixels from data. Density is the product.
        OWN-WORLD: Near-black rail as spatial anchor, off-white content. One blue accent,
        reserved for the primary action, the current selection and focus. Hairline
        borders. Six severity colours as dot + word, never colour alone. System sans for
        the UI, mono for data - no webfont on a self-hosted console.
        STORY: An engineer arrives with a question, narrows the field in three gestures
        (range, level, service), clicks a value in a cell to filter on it, opens a row
        without losing the search, copies a trace id, closes.
        FIRST VIEWPORT: 200px rail. Header with project selector and time range. Full
        width search. Filter row and active chips. Count and sort. Then the table:
        32px rows, sticky header, tabular-nums time, visually truncated message.
        FORM: Inherited from the approved direction in specs/mockups/ (spec 07.20),
        raised on three counts - finer hairlines, tighter type scale (1.125), tabular
        figures throughout the data columns.
        FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the
        finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md.
        -->
        {% block body %}{% endblock %}
    </body>
</html>
